IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gst-registration`
IMPORT `gst-formulas`

-- A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999, ss 9-80, 129-20, 129-40, 129-70, 129-75, 138-5 -- worked cases for
-- gst-formulas.l4 (24 October 2026).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were worked by hand from
-- the text and the formulas transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00446.formulas.md, before the encoding was run.
-- Every figure is hypothetical.

§ `s 9-80 -- partly GST-free supplies`

-- gst-cases-registration.l4's "$1,100 sale of which $440 is GST-free" (GST 60), asked from its taxable proportion instead: the
-- taxable part is worth 600 and the GST-free part 440, so the taxable proportion is 600 / 1,040 = 15/26. Value of the actual
-- supply: 1,100 x 10 / (10 + 15/26) = 11,000 x 26 / 275 = 1,040; GST: 10% of 1,040 x 15/26 = 60, the same answer.
#ASSERT `What is the value of my partly taxable supply` 1100 (15 DIVIDED BY 26) EQUALS 1040
#ASSERT `How much GST is on my partly taxable supply` 1100 (15 DIVIDED BY 26) EQUALS 60
-- Wholly taxable: 2,200 x 10 / 11 = 2,000, GST 200 (s 9-75 gives the same). Wholly GST-free: value 2,200, GST nil.
#ASSERT `What is the value of my partly taxable supply` 2200 1 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `How much GST is on my partly taxable supply` 2200 1 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `How much GST is on my partly taxable supply` 2200 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 129-20 -- adjustment periods`

-- Not business finance: $4,000 GST exclusive, 2 periods; $30,000, 5; $600,000, 10. Business finance: $30,000, 1; $100,000, 5.
#ASSERT `How many adjustment periods do I have` 4000 FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `How many adjustment periods do I have` 30000 FALSE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `How many adjustment periods do I have` 600000 FALSE EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many adjustment periods do I have` 30000 TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many adjustment periods do I have` 100000 TRUE EQUALS 5

§ `ss 129-40, 129-70, 129-75 -- change in creditable purpose`

-- A van bought for $33,000 including GST: full input tax credit 3,000. Claimed at 80% business use; actually 60% by the end of
-- the first adjustment period: increasing adjustment 3,000 x 20% = 600. Actually 90%: decreasing adjustment 3,000 x 10% = 300.
-- Actually 80%: none.
#ASSERT `What Division 129 adjustment do I have` 33000 FALSE 1 80 60 EQUALS `an increasing adjustment` 600
#ASSERT `What Division 129 adjustment do I have` 33000 FALSE 1 80 90 EQUALS `a decreasing adjustment` 300
#ASSERT `What Division 129 adjustment do I have` 33000 FALSE 1 80 80 EQUALS `no adjustment: the actual application is the same as the intended or former application`
-- The van ($30,000 GST exclusive) has 5 adjustment periods: the 5th still adjusts (former 60%, actual 50%: 300); the 6th does not.
#ASSERT `What Division 129 adjustment do I have` 33000 FALSE 5 60 50 EQUALS `an increasing adjustment` 300
#ASSERT `What Division 129 adjustment do I have` 33000 FALSE 6 60 50 EQUALS `no adjustment: this tax period is not one of the acquisition's adjustment periods`

§ `s 138-5 -- cancelling registration`

-- The van, 60% actual application, worth $22,000 including GST when registration is cancelled, bought for $33,000: the
-- consideration is not less than the market value, so the applicable value is 22,000; 1/11 x 60% x 22,000 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `What adjustment do I have on cancelling my registration` TRUE FALSE 60 22000 33000 EQUALS `an increasing adjustment on cancellation` 1200
-- Bought for $11,000, less than the $22,000 value: applicable value 11,000; 1/11 x 60% x 11,000 = 600.
#ASSERT `What adjustment do I have on cancelling my registration` TRUE FALSE 60 22000 11000 EQUALS `an increasing adjustment on cancellation` 600
-- Its last adjustment period already ended: none. No input tax credit for it: none.
#ASSERT `What adjustment do I have on cancelling my registration` TRUE TRUE 60 22000 33000 EQUALS `no adjustment: the last adjustment period for the thing ended before the cancellation (s 138-5(3))`
#ASSERT `What adjustment do I have on cancelling my registration` FALSE FALSE 60 22000 33000 EQUALS `no adjustment: I was never entitled to an input tax credit for the thing`
